#
# \brief  P2.1 RED scenario: sponge-de survival under package-control
#         failure (sponge_pkgd wedged/killed mid-operation).
# \author Sponge OS contributors
# \date   2026
#
# Contract: docs/evidence/phase16-runtime-de-failure-modes.md (P0.4
# failure-mode audit) - section 4 target degraded-state contract C1-C5,
# section 5 positive controls P1-P5 / negative controls N1-N6, section 6
# open questions Q1-Q3. Plan: docs/plans/phase16-runtime-overhaul.md
# P2.1 (this RED test) and P2.5 (the DE hardening that flips it green).
# Failure domain FD2 / decision D16R.7: the DE stays interactive and
# labeled; package-control failures are contained to the operation.
#
# RUN (serial runner only, D16R.13):
#
#   ./tool/build run sponge-de-pkgd-failure
#
# EXPECTED OUTCOME ON CURRENT CODE (the P2.1 RED receipt):
#
#   The scenario FAILS with the per-contract RED markers and WITHOUT
#   the green marker (N1):
#     de-survival-probe: [c4] RED - operation-error machine witness
#         absent ... (contract section 4 C4 gap: log-only transient
#         witness today; Q3 candidate channel)
#     de-survival-probe: [c5] RED - the failed operation's error is
#         not persistent ... (contract section 4 C5 ...)
#     de-survival-probe: verdict RED (c4 c5)
#   Everything else passes: the positive controls P1-P5, C1 (panel +
#   demo first paint, popup repaint during the degraded window), C2
#   (QMP input flip), C3 (health label `sponge_pkgd unresponsive(N)`
#   substrate - it is GREEN here because `system_state` is routed and
#   asserted by substring), and the C4/C5 log-side halves (the bounded
#   `launch problem` error and the <= 3 s feed-recovery window). The
#   RED lands exactly on the documented missing mechanisms: a stable,
#   probe-readable operation-error artifact (C4) and the error-stays-
#   visible-until-acknowledged / explicit degraded-recovered semantics
#   (C5). P2.5 lands those, this scenario flips to
#   `de-survival-probe: PASS` with no scenario edit (see the probe
#   header, Q3).
#
# WHAT THE SCENARIO WIRES (base: run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run,
# the proven QMP input + Qt6/Mesa softpipe template):
#
#   init
#   + timer
#   + report_rom        (relays every probe/DE/pkgd channel; policies
#                        below, including the `system -> config` config
#                        relay and `system -> state` -> `system_state`)
#   + nitpicker         (domains: panel 28px, launcher popup, demo
#                        window, default - same as the template)
#   + drivers           (sub-init: acpi -> report_rom -> pci_decode ->
#                        platform, vesa_fb, ps2, usb=pc_usb_host,
#                        usb_hid, event_filter - the real input chain)
#   + sponge-de         (Qt6 DE; <launcher source="pkgd"/> +
#                        <launcher_state source="report"/> + the
#                        `system_state` ROM route for the health label)
#   + pkg_runtime       (nested init hosting launched packages)
#   + cfg_probe         (bystander; the alpha_probe/cfg_probe health
#                        exclusion semantics are exercised defensively
#                        - see N3/Q1 in the probe header)
#   + system            (nested init; hosts sponge_pkgd so its state
#                        report is the health-watcher input; its config
#                        is the PROBE-OWNED relay, so the scenario can
#                        kill/wedge/revive pkgd by config version bumps
#                        - Start_model::matches() keys on name+version)
#   + de_survival_probe (the P2.1 probe; choreography + assertions)
#
# THE INJECTION (contract section 2.3 item 4: wedge/kill the pkgd child
# only, shared substrate healthy, heartbeat machinery accounted for):
# the probe publishes `system` config v2, which bumps sponge_pkgd's
# start-node version (init kills the healthy incarnation) and re-routes
# its `request` ROM to the unresolvable label `sponge_pkgd_wedge_denied`
# so the replacement incarnation sleeps forever in its first entrypoint-
# thread session open ("stop because parent denied"). Heartbeat skips
# accumulate (`+ heartbeat | rate_ms: 2000`, product-shaped
# `restart_after_skipped: 3 | restart_budget: 3`, short 3 s startup
# grace on the wedge incarnation), the health watcher composes
# `sponge_pkgd unresponsive(N)`, the churn settles (Q2 is OBSERVED and
# recorded by the probe), and config v3 revives pkgd. An in-flight
# `explain hello` request dies with the killed incarnation (P2.1:
# "wedge or kill sponge_pkgd during a package-control operation"; N5:
# it is never asserted for an answer).
#
# The degraded-window launch target is a package whose launcher_result
# never arrived (the menu is swapped pkg_gui_demo -> hello before the
# wedge): LauncherController::_poll_launch_result matches results by
# (op, pkg) only, so a re-launch of the pre-wedge package would be
# answered from the STALE launcher_result ROM and silently "succeed" -
# the scenario must witness the designed bounded timeout + structured
# error instead (contract section 3 mode C).
#
# CONTROLS ENFORCED BY THIS SCRIPT + THE PROBE:
#   P1  pre-wedge launch click -> sponge_pkgd: launch result
#       'pkg_gui_demo' -> ok (contract P1 allows the pkgd-side witness;
#       the DE's own 'launched' log races its 6 s result poll) +
#       pkg_gui_demo: window shown + green first paint (real input!)
#   P2  pre-wedge feed live    -> launcher report lists pkg_gui_demo
#       (corroborated by the `sponge-de: launcher list updated` log,
#       asserted post-hoc from the captured log)
#   P3  pre-wedge health label absent (derived warnings empty)
#   P4  post-recovery launch click -> launched 'pkg_gui_demo' again +
#       green pixel (pixels guard against the stale-result false PASS)
#   P5  QMP input witness during the degraded window (input report
#       press flip + popup repaint)
#   N1  green marker absent while RED (verdict block asserts it)
#   N2  substrate health: system_state keeps updating + the panel
#       keeps compositing through the window (C1b/C2 pixels) + the DE
#       answers input - a frozen substrate cannot produce those
#   N3  no alpha_probe/cfg_probe segment is ever asserted (probe
#       skip-list mirrors the DE exclusion predicate)
#   N4  no install/remove on the DE's launcher_request channel (the
#       probe's ops go through probe_request/probe_result)
#   N5  no assertion requires pkgd to answer while wedged
#   N6  health assertions are substring-only, never whole-label
#
# First paint + real input are mandatory evidence (D16R.11): the panel
# toggle + demo window pixels gate the pre-wedge phase, the popup
# repaints on a real QMP click inside the degraded window, and the
# pkg_gui_demo green pixel proves both launch halves. QEMU evidence
# only (D16R.12).
#

assert {[have_spec sel4]} \
	"sponge-de-pkgd-failure requires KERNEL=sel4 (BOARD=pc) in build.conf. \
	 This scenario drives the real PC input chain (vesa_fb/ps2/usb_hid); \
	 use run/sponge-de.run for the base-linux fb_sdl variant."

build { core lib/ld init timer server/report_rom server/nitpicker \
         driver/acpi app/pci_decode driver/platform \
         driver/framebuffer/vesa driver/ps2 \
         driver/usb_host/pc driver/usb_hid \
         server/event_filter \
         sponge_pkgd sponge-de cfg_probe pkg_hello \
         test/pkg_gui_demo test/de_survival_probe \
         qt6/base lib/libc lib/libm lib/stdcxx lib/mesa \
         lib/mesa_gpu-softpipe lib/egl lib/softpipe lib/libdrm lib/expat \
         lib/qt6_component lib/vfs lib/vfs_pipe lib/vfs_gpu lib/rom_filter \
         lib/zlib lib/libpng lib/blit }

create_boot_directory

install_config {
config
+ parent-provides
  + service ROM
  + service PD
  + service RM
  + service CPU
  + service LOG
  + service IRQ
  + service IO_MEM
  + service IO_PORT

+ default | caps: 200 | ram: 4M
+ default-route
  + any-service
    + parent
    + any-child

+ start timer
  + provides | + service Timer

#
# report_rom - the single relay. Policy labels use the FULL session
# label chains: pkgd lives one init deeper (`system`), so its sessions
# arrive as `system -> sponge_pkgd -> <label>` (the same chaining as
# the product's `pkg_runtime -> debug -> installed` policies,
# run/sponge-desktop-disk.run:650-652).
#
+ start report_rom | caps: 300 | ram: 8M
  + provides
    + service Report
    + service ROM
  + config | verbose: yes
    #
    # The system-sandbox config relay (the sponge_supervisor pattern,
    # run/supervisor.inc::sys_config_relay): the probe publishes the
    # nested init's config as the report `system_config`.
    #
    + policy | label: system -> config | report: de_survival_probe -> system_config
    #
    # The nested init's state report -> the health-watcher input ROM
    # (suffix matcher so the DE and the probe can both read it).
    #
    + policy | label_suffix: system_state | report: system -> state
    #
    # pkgd's channels. `request` is mapped to a NEVER-WRITTEN report
    # label so the always-open ROM is empty (pkgd idles; the
    # run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run trick). launcher_request is
    # the DE's launch-only writer channel (N4: the probe never writes
    # install/remove there). probe_request/probe_result are the
    # probe's own transport.
    #
    + policy | label: system -> sponge_pkgd -> request          | report: de_survival_probe -> idle_request
    + policy | label: system -> sponge_pkgd -> probe_request    | report: de_survival_probe -> probe_request
    + policy | label: system -> sponge_pkgd -> launcher_request | report: sponge-de -> launcher_request
    + policy | label: de_survival_probe -> probe_result | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> probe_result
    + policy | label: de_survival_probe -> installed    | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> installed
    + policy | label: sponge-de -> installed            | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> installed
    + policy | label: sponge-de -> launcher_result      | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> launcher_result
    + policy | label: pkg_runtime -> config             | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> runtime
    + policy | label: cfg_probe -> config               | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> runtime
    #
    # sponge-de's reports -> the probe's witnesses.
    #
    + policy | label: de_survival_probe -> sponge_de_input | report: sponge-de -> input
    + policy | label: de_survival_probe -> launcher_state | report: sponge-de -> launcher_state
    + policy | label: de_survival_probe -> launcher       | report: sponge-de -> launcher
    #
    # C4/C5 candidate operation-error artifact (Q3): empty until P2.5
    # makes sponge-de write it - the probe asserts against this ROM.
    #
    + policy | label: de_survival_probe -> de_op_error    | report: sponge-de -> de_op_error

+ start nitpicker | ram: 16M
  + provides
    + service Gui
    + service Capture
    + service Event
  + route
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child
  + config
    + capture
    + event
    + domain panel | layer: 1 | content: client | label: no
                   | hover: always | focus: click | ypos: 0 | height: 28
    + domain launcher | layer: 0 | content: client | label: no
                      | hover: always | focus: click
                      | xpos: 0 | ypos: 28 | width: 341 | height: 480
    + domain demo | layer: 2 | content: client | label: no
                  | hover: always | focus: click
                  | xpos: 192 | ypos: 172 | width: 640 | height: 480
    + domain default | layer: 3 | content: client | label: no
                     | hover: always | focus: click | ypos: 28 | height: -28
    + policy | label_prefix: sponge-de -> Sponge Panel   | domain: panel
    + policy | label_prefix: sponge-de -> Sponge Launcher | domain: launcher
    + policy | label_prefix: sponge-de -> Sponge DE Demo | domain: demo
    + default-policy | domain: default
    + background | color: #1e1e2e

+ start drivers | caps: 1500 | ram: 96M | managing_system: yes
  + binary init
  + route
    + service ROM | label: config | + parent | label: drivers.config
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + service Capture | + child nitpicker
    + service Event | + child nitpicker
    + any-service                 | + parent
  + config
    + parent-provides
      + service IRQ
      + service IO_MEM
      + service IO_PORT
      + service ROM
      + service PD
      + service RM
      + service CPU
      + service LOG
      + service Timer
      + service Capture
      + service Event

    + default | caps: 60

    + start acpi | caps: 250 | ram: 4M
      + route
        + service IO_MEM | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service RM | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service Report | + child report_rom

    + start report_rom | caps: 100 | ram: 2M
      + provides
      | + service ROM
      | + service Report
      + config
      | + policy | label: pci_decode -> system | report: acpi -> acpi
      | + policy | label: platform -> devices  | report: pci_decode -> devices
      | + policy | label: usb_hid -> report    | report: usb -> devices
      + route
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent

    + start pci_decode | caps: 100 | ram: 2M
      + route
        + service Report | + child report_rom
        + service ROM | label: system | + child report_rom
        + service IO_MEM | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service RM | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent

    + start platform | caps: 200 | ram: 3M | managing_system: yes
      + provides
      | + service Dma
      | + service Platform
      + route
      | + service ROM | label: devices | + child report_rom
      | + service Report | + child report_rom
      | + service IRQ | + parent
      | + service IO_MEM | + parent
      | + service IO_PORT | + parent
      | + service ROM | + parent
      | + service PD | + parent
      | + service CPU | + parent
      | + service LOG | + parent
      | + service Timer | + parent
      + config
        + report | devices: yes
        + policy | label_prefix: ps2             | + device ps2
        + policy | label_prefix: fb  | info: yes | + pci | class: VGA
        + policy | label_prefix: usb | info: yes | + pci | class: USB

    + start fb | caps: 150 | ram: 20M
      + binary vesa_fb
      + route
        + service ROM | label: config | + parent | label: fb.config
        + service Report | + child report_rom
        + service Dma | + child platform
        + service Platform | + child platform
        + service IO_PORT | + parent
        + service IO_MEM | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service Timer | + parent
        + service Capture | + parent

    + start ps2 | caps: 100 | ram: 1280K
      + config
      + route
        + service Dma | + child platform
        + service Platform | + child platform
        + service Event | + child event_filter | label: ps2
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service Timer | + parent

    + start usb | caps: 200 | ram: 16M
      + binary pc_usb_host
      + provides | + service Usb
      + config
      | + report | devices: yes
      | + policy | label_prefix: usb_hid | + device | class: 0x3
      + route
        + service Dma | + child platform
        + service Platform | + child platform
        + service Report | label: devices | + child report_rom
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service RM | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service Timer | + parent

    + start usb_hid | caps: 180 | ram: 10M
      + route
        + service ROM | label: report | + child report_rom
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service RM | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service Timer | + parent
        + service Event | + child event_filter | label: usb
        + service Usb | + child usb

    + start event_filter | caps: 90 | ram: 1280K
      + provides | + service Event
      + route
        + service ROM | label: config | + parent | label: event_filter.config
        + service Event | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service Timer | + parent

#
# sponge-de - the Qt6 DE. Launcher wired to pkgd (the installed
# broadcast + the launch-only launcher_request/launcher_result pair),
# launcher_state report ON (the C2 flip witness), system_state ROM
# routed (C3 health label; Optional_rom_dataspace keeps it non-fatal).
#
+ start sponge-de | caps: 1000 | ram: 128M
  + config
    + launcher | source: pkgd
    + launcher_state | source: report
    + vfs
      + dir dev
        + log
        + inline rtc | : 2018-01-01 00:01
      + dir pipe | + pipe
      + tar qt6_dejavusans.tar
      + tar qt6_libqgenode.tar
    + libc | stdout: /dev/log | stderr: /dev/log | pipe: /pipe | rtc: /dev/rtc
  + route
    + service Gui | label_last: Sponge Panel   | + child nitpicker
    + service Gui | label_last: Sponge Launcher | + child nitpicker
    + service Gui | + child nitpicker
    + service Report | label: shape  | + child report_rom
    + service Report | label: input  | + child report_rom
    + service Report | label: launcher          | + child report_rom
    + service Report | label: launcher_request  | + child report_rom
    + service Report | label: launcher_state    | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: installed            | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: launcher_result      | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: system_state         | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: default.theme        | + parent
    + service ROM | label: mesa_gpu.lib.so | + parent | label: mesa_gpu-softpipe.lib.so
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# pkg_runtime - nested init hosting launched packages (same shape as
# run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run: Gui straight to nitpicker, no wm).
#
+ start pkg_runtime | caps: 2000 | ram: 256M
  + binary init
  + route
    + service ROM | label: config                 | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: mesa_gpu.lib.so   | + parent | label: mesa_gpu-softpipe.lib.so
    + service Gui | + child nitpicker
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# cfg_probe - the product-shaped bystander (its clean exits are in the
# health-watcher exclusion pair, so it also exercises the N3 exclusion
# semantics without polluting the assertions). Event-driven log lines,
# kept as corroboration only.
#
+ start cfg_probe | caps: 100 | ram: 4M
  + route
    + service ROM | label: config | + child report_rom
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# system - the nested sandbox that hosts sponge_pkgd. Its CONFIG comes
# from the probe's `system_config` report (the relay policy above), so
# the scenario can kill/wedge/revive pkgd by publishing config v1/v2/v3
# (start-node version bumps; Start_model::matches() is name+version).
# Its STATE report (`system -> state`) is the health-watcher input.
#
# pool covers the init's own overhead + pkgd's 400 + a full restart
# margin (observed with caps: 200: slack=13 and restarts clamped to
# "configured caps exceed available caps, proceed with 51", which left
# the child unable to create signal contexts - permanent wedge).
+ start system | caps: 800 | ram: 64M
  + binary init
  + route
    + service ROM | label: config | + child report_rom
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + service ROM | label_last: request          | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: probe_request    | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: launcher_request | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent

#
# de_survival_probe - the P2.1 probe. Observe-only (Capture + Timer +
# report_rom channels; no Event session - the input is real QMP).
#
+ start de_survival_probe | caps: 200 | ram: 16M
  + config | render_iters: 9000
  + route
    + service Capture | + child nitpicker
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + service ROM | label: sponge_de_input | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: launcher_state  | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: launcher        | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: installed       | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: system_state    | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: probe_result    | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: de_op_error     | + child report_rom
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child
- }

#
# Stage every non-build-artifact boot module into bin/ BEFORE
# build_boot_image (on base-sel4 the boot image is a single packed
# image.elf; modules added later never reach the guest - the same
# staging recipe as run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run).
#
exec mkdir -p bin

set dejavu_dst "bin/qt6_dejavusans.tar"
if {![file exists $dejavu_dst]} {
	set dejavu_src [glob -nocomplain "${genode_dir}/contrib/qt6_base-*/src/lib/qt6_base/src/3rdparty/wasm/DejaVuSans.ttf"]
	if {[llength $dejavu_src] == 0} {
		error "DejaVuSans.ttf not found in the qt6_base port sources"
	}
	set staging "[run_dir]/dejavusans-staging"
	file mkdir "$staging/qt/lib/fonts"
	file copy -force [lindex $dejavu_src 0] "$staging/qt/lib/fonts/DejaVuSans.ttf"
	exec tar -cf $dejavu_dst -C $staging qt
	file delete -force $staging
}

set recipe_dir "${genode_dir}/repos/os/recipes/raw/drivers_interactive-pc"
foreach f { drivers.config fb.config } {
	if {![file exists "$recipe_dir/$f"]} {
		error "$recipe_dir/$f missing (vendored drivers_interactive-pc recipe drifted?)"
	}
	exec cp -f "$recipe_dir/$f" "bin/$f"
}

#
# event_filter.config - WRITTEN (not copied) with the two proven
# deviations of the template: no <accelerate> wrapper on the ps2 input
# (1:1 rel mapping for the PS/2 click recipe) and a <transform> scale
# on the usb input (QEMU usb-tablet device units -> 1024x768 pixels).
# See run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run for the full rationale.
#
set ef_fh [open "bin/event_filter.config" w]
puts $ef_fh {config
+ output
  + chargen
    + merge
    | + transform
    | | + scale | x: 0.0312517 | y: 0.0234382
    | | + input usb
    + button-scroll
    | |   + input ps2
    | |   + vertical   | button: BTN_MIDDLE | speed_percent: -10
    | |   + horizontal | button: BTN_MIDDLE | speed_percent: -10
  + mod1
  | + key KEY_LEFTSHIFT
  | + key KEY_RIGHTSHIFT
  + mod2
  | + key KEY_LEFTCTRL
  | + key KEY_RIGHTCTRL
  + mod3
  | + key KEY_RIGHTALT | . AltGr
  + repeat | delay_ms: 230 | rate_ms: 90
  + include | rom: en_us.chargen
  + include | rom: special.chargen
+ policy | label: ps2 | input: ps2
+ policy | label: usb | input: usb
-}
close $ef_fh

set chargen_dir "${genode_dir}/repos/os/src/server/event_filter"
foreach f { en_us.chargen special.chargen } {
	if {![file exists "$chargen_dir/$f"]} {
		error "$chargen_dir/$f missing (event_filter sources drifted?)"
	}
	exec cp -f "$chargen_dir/$f" "bin/$f"
}

exec cp -f "${genode_dir}/repos/sponge/src/sponge-de/themes/default.theme" \
           "bin/default.theme"

#
# Stage package metadata + the derived index. pkg_gui_demo is the
# launch target (green first paint); hello is the degraded-window
# FRESH launch target and the swap package (its metadata declares
# <autostart/>, which is fine - it only ever installs while pkgd is
# healthy or after revival). Same scheme as run/sponge-launch.run.
#
set staged_pkgs { pkg_gui_demo hello }
foreach pkg $staged_pkgs {
	set src "${genode_dir}/../pkg/$pkg/metadata.xml"
	if {![file exists $src]} {
		error "package metadata not found: $src"
	}
	exec cp -L $src "bin/pkg_$pkg.xml"
}

set index_fh [open "bin/pkg_index.xml" w]
puts $index_fh "<packages>"
foreach pkg $staged_pkgs {
	puts $index_fh "  <pkg name=\"$pkg\"/>"
}
puts $index_fh "</packages>"
close $index_fh

#
# Full boot module list. [build_artifacts] provides the shared libs
# (egl.lib.so, expat.lib.so, the Qt libs, ... - inherently artifact
# tracked and validated by check_for_missing_lib_build); the explicit
# names below make the list DETERMINISTIC against a flaky artifact
# harvest on the shared build dir (observed 2026-10-28: successive warm
# makes recorded different artifact sets - run1 missed the Qt libs,
# run3 missed core-sel4.a - the D16R.13 concurrent-make hazard).
# Kernel-variant names are the ones the boot_dir/sel4 staging
# normalizes (core-sel4.a -> linked as core.a, ld-sel4.lib.so ->
# ld.lib.so, hpet_timer -> timer). Duplicates from the harvest are
# harmless (copy_file -force).
#
set boot_modules [build_artifacts]
foreach m { core-sel4.a ld-sel4.lib.so hpet_timer \
            init report_rom nitpicker \
            acpi pci_decode platform vesa_fb ps2 pc_usb_host usb_hid event_filter \
            sponge_pkgd sponge-de cfg_probe hello pkg_gui_demo de_survival_probe \
            libQt6Core.lib.so libQt6Gui.lib.so libQt6Widgets.lib.so \
            libqgenode.lib.so qt6_libqgenode.tar qt6_dejavusans.tar \
            drivers.config fb.config event_filter.config \
            en_us.chargen special.chargen \
            default.theme \
            pkg_pkg_gui_demo.xml pkg_hello.xml pkg_index.xml } {
	lappend boot_modules $m
}

#
# Dedicated build pass recording exactly the artifact-tracked names the
# stage check validates (every *.lib.so boot module must appear as a
# BUILD_ARTIFACTS entry of the `build` step): ld-sel4.lib.so via
# lib/ld and the Qt libs via qt6/base. The combined build above does
# not reliably re-record them on warm trees (see the header comment of
# the boot-module list); a dedicated make re-runs the import steps and
# the `build` proc accumulates the entries - verified empirically
# (progress.log after `make qt6/base` carries libQt6Core.lib.so ..
# qt6_libqgenode.tar).
#
build { core lib/ld qt6/base }

build_boot_image $boot_modules

#
# QEMU: base-sel4 needs >= 1 GiB guest RAM; 2G matches the template
# (pkg_runtime 256M + a second Qt6/Mesa softpipe renderer).
# -nographic keeps it headless (serial only). The nec-usb-xhci +
# usb-tablet give the absolute pointer usb_hid binds.
#
source [file join [file dirname [file normalize [info script]]] qmp.inc]

#
# Entry-click dispatch: matches the probe's `QMP-TARGET entry <x> <y>`
# marker (the capture-located launcher-button center) and routes it
# through qmp_tablet_click (the usb-tablet abs recipe). Unlike
# qmp_exec_target_launch_click, which hard-codes (170,120), this takes
# the probe-observed coordinates - the popup geometry drifts between
# boots (QPA geometry.topLeft (0,0)/(0,28) shift, qmp.inc header +
# docs/evidence/task-3b-phase12-launch-click.md), so a fixed target is
# not reliable here.
#
proc de_tablet_click { chan tx ty } {
	set idx [qmp_tablet_index $chan]
	if {$idx eq ""} {
		puts stderr "\nFAIL: query-mice shows no absolute mouse device"
		exit 1
	}
	qmp_hmp $chan "mouse_set $idx"
	set ax [expr {($tx * 32767 + 512) / 1024}]
	set ay [expr {($ty * 32767 + 384) / 768}]
	qmp_cmd $chan [format {{"execute":"input-send-event","arguments":{"events":[{"type":"abs","data":{"axis":"x","value":%d}},{"type":"abs","data":{"axis":"y","value":%d}}]}}} $ax $ay]
	after 15
	qmp_hmp $chan "mouse_button 1"
	after 15
	qmp_hmp $chan "mouse_button 0"
}


proc dispatch_sequence { chan timeout_s } {
	global qemu_spawn_id output
	if {![info exists qemu_spawn_id]} {
		puts stderr "\nFAIL: qemu_spawn_id not set for dispatch_sequence"
		exit 1
	}
	set timeout $timeout_s
	match_max -i $qemu_spawn_id 200000
	while {1} {
		expect {
			-i $qemu_spawn_id
			-re {QMP-TARGET entry (-?\d+) (-?\d+)\r*\n} {
				set ex $expect_out(1,string)
				set ey $expect_out(2,string)
				# Save the outer scan before the nested press wait
				# replaces expect_out. This region may contain markers
				# needed by subsequent history-aware gates.
				append output $expect_out(buffer)
				set done_pending 0
				#
				# Press-verified tablet click with retries: the
				# button events drop intermittently on this host
				# (run14) and qmp_hmp swallows HMP errors; the DE's
				# own input report is the only landing signal. A
				# landed click always produces a press, so a toggle
				# can never be double-flipped by the retry.
				#
				set timeout 5
				for {set attempt 1} {$attempt <= 3} {incr attempt} {
					puts "\nqmp: dispatching entry click at ($ex,$ey) via usb-tablet abs (attempt $attempt)"
					de_tablet_click $chan $ex $ey
					set got_press 0
					expect {
						-i $qemu_spawn_id
						-re {(QMP-TARGET done|<input press=)} {
							# One pattern is required: separate Expect
							# arms are tried in pattern order, so a press
							# arm can consume an earlier done as scan text.
							if {$expect_out(1,string) eq "QMP-TARGET done"} {
								set done_pending 1
								exp_continue -continue_timer
							}
							set got_press 1
						}
						-re {de-survival-probe: FAIL.*\r*\n} {
							puts stderr "\nFAIL - probe reported failure during click"
							exit 1
						}
						timeout { }
					}
					append output $expect_out(buffer)
					if {$got_press} {
						puts "\nqmp: entry click confirmed by input press"
						break
					}
					puts "\nqmp: no input press after entry click attempt $attempt - retrying"
					after 300
				}
				set timeout $timeout_s
				if {$done_pending} {
					puts "\nqmp: sequence done"
					return
				}
			}
			-re {QMP-TARGET done\r*\n} {
				puts "\nqmp: sequence done"
				append output $expect_out(buffer)
				return
			}
			-re {de-survival-probe: FAIL.*\r*\n} {
				puts stderr "\nFAIL - probe reported failure"
				exit 1
			}
			timeout {
				puts stderr "\nFAIL - no sequence marker within ${timeout_s}s"
				exit 1
			}
		}
	}
}


append qemu_args " -nographic -m 2G "
append qemu_args " -device nec-usb-xhci,id=xhci -device usb-tablet "

#
# Gate plan. Gates 1-2 verify the driver substrate on throwaway boots
# (the run tool respawns QEMU per run_genode_until call without a
# spawn id). Gate 3 starts the SINGLE long-lived boot the probe's
# whole choreography runs in; every later gate chains on that spawn.
#
run_genode_until {.*\[init -> drivers -> fb\] using 1024x768} 300
run_genode_until {.*Connected device.*QEMU QEMU USB Tablet.*POINTER} 300

set qmp_port [qmp_pick_port]
append qemu_args " -qmp tcp:127.0.0.1:${qmp_port},server=on,wait=off "

run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[boot\] ok} 1200
# The first two driver gates use throwaway boots. Require the tablet
# on this long-lived boot too before any QMP click is attempted.
run_genode_until {.*Connected device.*QEMU QEMU USB Tablet.*POINTER} 300 $qemu_spawn_id

set qmp_chan [qmp_connect $qmp_port]
global qemu_spawn_id
#
# Raise the expect match-window for the QEMU serial stream BEFORE any
# further expect block can consume data (the poll-spam match_max root
# cause documented in docs/evidence/task-2-phase10-interactive.md).
#
match_max -i $qemu_spawn_id 200000

#
# Capture the serial stream for the post-hoc contract receipt (the
# upgrade-wedge pattern, run/sponge-upgrade-wedge.run).
#
set de_log "[run_dir]/sponge-de-pkgd-failure.log"
log_file -a $de_log

#
# dispatch_sequence must scan past unrelated serial lines while looking
# for QMP markers. It appends everything it consumes to the run tool's
# global output history, so a later gate first checks that history
# instead of timing out on a marker that has already gone by.
#
rename run_genode_until de_stock_run_genode_until
proc run_genode_until {args} {
	global output
	if {[regexp [lindex $args 0] $output]} {
		return
	}
	set result [uplevel 1 [list de_stock_run_genode_until {*}$args]]
	return $result
}

#
# P2/P3/C1 (pre-wedge substrate + positive controls). The flow is
# driven by the probe's strictly-ordered markers; the
# `sponge-de: launcher list updated` feed log is asserted post-hoc
# from the captured log (its interleaving with the probe markers is
# inherently racy - the DE polls at 1500 ms).
#
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[install\] ok} 120 $qemu_spawn_id
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[p2\] ok} 60 $qemu_spawn_id
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[p3\] ok} 60 $qemu_spawn_id
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[c1\] ok} 60 $qemu_spawn_id

#
# P1: pre-wedge launch click over the real input path. S-toggle click
# (PS/2 recipe) opens the popup; the entry click goes through the
# proven usb-tablet recipe (dispatch_entry_click uses the probe-located
# coordinates - see its header; the old fixed-landing helper at
# (170,120)); the green pixel + `window shown` are the real-launch
# evidence (D16R.11). The green-pixel marker is the synchronization
# gate: dispatch_sequence may consume the earlier pkgd/window lines
# while waiting for QMP-TARGET done, so those lines are asserted from
# the captured log instead of gated a second time.
#
dispatch_sequence $qmp_chan 300
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[p1\] ok - popup opened} 300 $qemu_spawn_id
dispatch_sequence $qmp_chan 600
match_max -i $qemu_spawn_id 200000
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[p1\] ok - pkg_gui_demo green} 600 $qemu_spawn_id
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[p1\] ok - popup closed} 60 $qemu_spawn_id

#
# Menu swap (pkg_gui_demo -> hello) + the injection.
#
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[swap\] ok} 120 $qemu_spawn_id
dispatch_sequence $qmp_chan 300
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[wedge\] injected} 60 $qemu_spawn_id

#
# C3: the health-label substrate (substring witness). The probe may
# spend 45 s on each of three wedge publishes; the host gate must not
# cut off that documented retry sequence.
#
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[c3\] ok} 240 $qemu_spawn_id

#
# C2/P5: QMP input during the degraded window (press flip + popup
# repaint). The probe keeps the popup window short so the C4 entry
# click follows immediately.
#
dispatch_sequence $qmp_chan 300
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[c2\] ok} 300 $qemu_spawn_id

#
# C4: the DE's launch op into the wedge. The bounded structured error
# (the log half of C4 - green today) must surface within the ~6 s
# poll timeout; the machine-readable half is the probe's RED item.
#
dispatch_sequence $qmp_chan 300
match_max -i $qemu_spawn_id 200000
run_genode_until {.*launch problem surfaced on the panel: launch 'hello' failed: no answer from the package manager} 30 $qemu_spawn_id
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[c4\] (RED|ok)} 120 $qemu_spawn_id

#
# Q2: the restart-churn outcome observation (contract section 6).
#
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[q2\] (settled|bounded)} 120 $qemu_spawn_id

#
# Recovery + C5 (the feed window and the label clear are measured
# probe-side; the `launcher list updated` lines are asserted post-hoc).
#
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[recovery\]} 60 $qemu_spawn_id
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[c5\] (ok|RED) - installed republicated} 180 $qemu_spawn_id
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[c5\] (ok|RED) - health label} 30 $qemu_spawn_id
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[c5\] (ok|RED) - menu repopulated} 60 $qemu_spawn_id

#
# P4: post-recovery launch click. The probe closes any leftover popup
# first (its marker is dispatched below), then S + entry; the green
# pixel is the real-re-launch witness (the stale-result false-PASS
# guard).
#
dispatch_sequence $qmp_chan 300
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[p4\] ok - popup opened} 300 $qemu_spawn_id
dispatch_sequence $qmp_chan 600
match_max -i $qemu_spawn_id 200000
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[p4\] ok - pkg_gui_demo green} 600 $qemu_spawn_id
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: \[p4\] ok - popup closed} 60 $qemu_spawn_id

#
# Final verdict marker (always emitted - green or red).
#
run_genode_until {.*de-survival-probe: verdict } 120 $qemu_spawn_id

qmp_disconnect $qmp_chan
log_file

#
# Contract receipt (post-hoc assertions over the captured serial log).
#
set fd [open $de_log r]
set de_out [read $fd]
close $fd

set has_green_marker [regexp {de-survival-probe: PASS} $de_out]
set n_listed   [regexp -all {sponge-de: launcher list updated} $de_out]
set n_launched [regexp -all {sponge_pkgd: launch result pkg_gui_demo -> ok} $de_out]
set n_windows  [regexp -all {pkg_gui_demo: window shown} $de_out]
set has_problem [regexp {launch problem surfaced on the panel: launch 'hello' failed: no answer from the package manager} $de_out]
set red_c4 [regexp {de-survival-probe: \[c4\] RED} $de_out]
set red_c5 [regexp {de-survival-probe: \[c5\] RED} $de_out]

puts "\nde-survival-probe: ---- P2.1 contract receipt (QEMU-labeled, D16R.12) ----"
puts "de-survival-probe: c1 panel/demo first paint ....... witnessed (probe pixels)"
puts "de-survival-probe: c2 QMP input in degraded window  witnessed (press flip + popup)"
puts "de-survival-probe: c3 health label substrate ....... witnessed (substring)"
if {$has_problem} {
	puts "de-survival-probe: c4 bounded structured error .... witnessed (launch problem log)"
} else {
	puts "de-survival-probe: c4 bounded structured error .... MISSING (gate failed)"
}
if {$red_c4} {
	puts "de-survival-probe: c4 machine-readable witness .... RED (documented P0.4 section 4 C4 gap)"
} else {
	puts "de-survival-probe: c4 machine-readable witness .... ok"
}
puts "de-survival-probe: c5 feed recovery window ......... measured probe-side (see \[c5\] markers)"
if {$red_c5} {
	puts "de-survival-probe: c5 error persistence / state .... RED (documented P0.4 section 4 C5 gap)"
} else {
	puts "de-survival-probe: c5 error persistence / state .... ok"
}
puts "de-survival-probe: p1/p4 launch clicks .............. launched x$n_launched, windows x$n_windows (expect 2 each), feed updates x$n_listed (expect >= 3)"
if {$has_green_marker} {
	puts "de-survival-probe: n1 green marker ................ present (scenario GREEN)"
} else {
	puts "de-survival-probe: n1 green marker ................ absent - the P2.1 red gate holds (marker de-survival-probe:PASS deliberately not printed here)"
}

if {!$has_problem} {
	puts "de-survival-probe: FAIL - the bounded structured error never surfaced (harness or DE regression)"
	exit 1
}

if {$n_launched != 2 || $n_windows != 2 || $n_listed < 3} {
	puts "de-survival-probe: FAIL - launch/window/feed positive controls are incomplete (harness or DE regression)"
	exit 1
}

if {$has_green_marker} {
	puts "de-survival-probe: scenario GREEN (P2.5 mechanisms present)"
	exit 0
}

puts "\nde-survival-probe: scenario RED - expected before P2.5: c4 machine-readable error artifact + c5 error-persistence/explicit degraded-recovery semantics are absent (contract section 4)."
puts "de-survival-probe: See the per-item markers above; the red receipt is this log."
exit 1
